# Scripted events for the "lifts" recording (single notes), in ms on the recording's clock.
# With the settings export's switch assignments (Switch 2 and the right footswitch Transpose Up, the
# left footswitch Transpose Down), the first part transposes while a note is held, and returns to no
# transposition. The second part makes the left footswitch a sustain pedal through microLinn's NRPN
# importing, presses it while a note is held, and puts things back.

45200   switch 2 150         # Switch 2: Transpose Up, a note held (44.75-46.65 s)
105500  pedal right down     # Transpose Up, a note held (105.15-107.75 s)
105800  pedal right up
106600  pedal left down      # Transpose Down, twice: back to no transposition
106900  pedal left up
107200  pedal left down
107500  pedal left up

127000  set importing 1
127100  nrpn 230 2           # Global Foot Left Assignment: Sustain
128000  pedal left down      # a note held (127.75-129.4 s)
131000  pedal left up
132000  midi B0 63 01 B0 62 66 B0 06 00 B0 26 12   # NRPN 230 = 18: the left footswitch back to Transpose Down
132100  set importing 0
